        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel issues fresh evacuation orders in south Lebanon despite ceasefire Middle East Issued on: 26/05/2026 - 17:30 Modified: 26/05/2026 - 17:32 Israel has issued an evacuation order for residents in the southern Lebanese town of Nabatiyeh, warning of fresh strikes against Hezbollah, despite a ceasefire. It comes after Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu promised to intensify attacks on Lebanon, following the killing of another Israeli soldier by a fibre optic drone sent by Hezbollah. Iran looking to 'buy time to rebuild its military' amid talks to end war 26/05/2026 Middle East US anxious to come to deal with Iran asTehran seeks release of frozen assets 26/05/2026 Middle East Palestine's Eid dampened by consequences of war on livestock 26/05/2026 Middle East Israel strikes Lebanese village and calls up more troops in the region 26/05/2026 Middle East US strikes Iranian targets amid agreement talks 26/05/2026 Americas US military sais it carried 'self-defense' strikes in first since ceasefire 26/05/2026 Middle East Nuclear issue remains key obstacle in Iran-US deal 25/05/2026 Middle East Millions gather in Mecca for Hajj despite security concerns 25/05/2026 Middle East Middle East: Deep mistrust clouds US-Iran negotiations 25/05/2026 Middle East"
